       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. The most per dose is typically 1,000 mg for IR, or 850 mg when dosing TID.\n- **Risk:** This is twice the daily maximum. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg PO BID with meals\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO BID or TID, or another regimen\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg TID, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
